{"id": "1204dfd1b9ea843f07c81242e21cf028df00d440072654c37bef7aa9c603b751", "source": "help_community", "source_type": "discussion", "source_id": "465678857_20", "url": "https://support.google.com/photos/thread/465678857?hl=en", "text": "tab on Android: 1.Verify Group Similar Faces Status: Open Google Photos, tap your Profile icon &gt; Photos settings &gt; Preferences &gt; Group similar faces, and ensure Face grouping is turned ON. 2.Re-label Unnamed Faces: Go to the Collections (or Search) tab, select People &amp; pets, tap a face, choose Add a name at the top, and type the person's name. 3.Search via the Main Search Bar: Instead of searching directly inside the People tab, tap the main Search icon at the bottom, type the assigned name in the search bar, and press enter. 4.Clear App Cache and Updates: Go to Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Photos &gt; Storage &amp; cache, tap Clear Cache, or go to the three dots at the top right and select Uninstall updates to reset glitched features. &nbsp;", "created_at": null, "is_reply": true, "parent_id": "465678857", "context": "Not able to search names on the people and faces tab", "category": "photos_searching", "text_completeness": "full"}
